      "syllabus": "The Mississippi Bar v. Charlene Mauk-Williams Majority Opinion: Griffis, J. Disposition: Charlene Mauk-Williams is hereby disbarred from the practice of law in the State of Mississippi, and her name shall be immediately removed from the rolls of the Mississippi Bar. Mauk-Williams is assessed all costs of this disciplinary proceeding. See Miss. R. Discipline 25. Charlene Mauk-Williams taxed with costs. Votes: Randolph, C.J., Kitchens and King, P.JJ., Coleman, Maxwell, Beam, Chamberlin and Ishee, JJ., Concur."
